{
  "rules": [
    "Apply a strong downward correction of -15% to -20% when the model forecast is based on recent history containing a negative sentiment spike (-1.0) followed by neutral sentiment, as models consistently overestimate downside recovery.",
    "Reduce forecasted volatility by 40-50% during periods where sentiment remains flat (0.00) for 7+ days; true outcomes show significantly lower amplitude swings than predicted.",
    "Shift the entire 30-day forecast curve downward by approximately 8-12 EUR when the last 3 days of history are below 62.50 and sentiment is neutral, indicating a structural bearish drift ignored by linear models.",
    "Expect mean reversion to occur within 14 days if the model predicts a sustained decline; true outcomes typically stabilize or rise sharply after hitting local lows (e.g., 52-53 EUR range).",
    "Ignore sentiment spikes in the forecast window entirely; neutral sentiment history dominates price action, causing models to overreact to isolated negative events."
  ]
}
